<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN" "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>This table exports statically resolved CodeQL Java source call sites: method
calls, explicit object creation, and <code>this</code> or <code>super</code>
constructor invocations. The Java model can include implicit superclass
constructor invocations. Functional-object creation nodes for lambdas and method
references are excluded; calls modeled inside their bodies retain their own
enclosing callable. Extractor-generated invocations of initializer holder methods
are excluded; source calls within initializer bodies are retained.</p>
<p>Caller and callee are normalized to source declarations. A virtual call records
the statically selected declaration, which can be an interface or superclass
method. It does not enumerate or predict its runtime dispatch targets. Reflection,
native implementations and unresolved calls are not reconstructed.</p>
<p>The columns, in order, are <code>caller_id</code>,
<code>caller_declaring_type</code>, <code>caller_signature</code>,
<code>callee_id</code>, <code>callee_declaring_type</code>,
<code>callee_signature</code>, <code>call_kind</code>, <code>source_path</code>,
<code>start_line</code>, <code>start_column</code>, <code>end_line</code> and
<code>end_column</code>. Call kinds are <code>method</code>, <code>new</code>,
<code>this-constructor</code> and <code>super-constructor</code>. Locations are
call-site locations; implicit calls use their extractor-assigned location.</p>
<p>Opaque identities combine declaring type, callable kind and signature, adding
source path and declaration position for source-backed callables. Binary targets
have semantic identities without a source anchor. These are database-snapshot
identities, not globally stable binary symbols. Paths are relative to the database
source root; coordinates are one-based and inclusive. Rows are ordered by source
path, source span, caller identity, callee identity and call kind.</p>
</overview>
<recommendation>
<p>Use these edges as static dependency evidence with the database's extraction
coverage in mind. Do not treat them as an exact or complete dynamic call graph.
Decode BQRS as CSV for downstream processing. This table is excluded from the M3
problem-query suite.</p>
</recommendation>
</qhelp>
